  "title": "Tokugawa shogunate",
  "summary": "The Tokugawa shogunate was a military government that ruled Japan from 1603 to 1868, after Tokugawa Ieyasu led a coalition of lords to victory in 1600. Governing from Edo, it required lords to spend alternate years in the capital and restricted contact with foreign countries. Its 250 years of secluded peace followed long civil wars and fostered a vibrant urban culture. A coup in the name of the young Emperor Meiji removed it from power.",
